        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2,\\ y=1$.",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by $3$, then add the first equation to eliminate $y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}12x-3y&=21\\\\13x&=26\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2+3y&=5\\\\y&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2+3(1)&=5\\\\4(2)-1&=7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
