          },
          "worked": "Double the first equation, then subtract the second equation to eliminate $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-6y&=-4\\\\-7y&=-12\\\\y&=\\frac{12}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into $x=3y-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=3\\left(\\frac{12}{7}\\right)-2\\\\x&=\\frac{36}{7}-\\frac{14}{7}\\\\x&=\\frac{22}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{22}{7}-3\\left(\\frac{12}{7}\\right)&=-2\\\\2\\left(\\frac{22}{7}\\right)+\\frac{12}{7}&=8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
