        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{9}{4},\\ y=\\frac{17}{8}$.",
          "worked": "Add the equations to eliminate $y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8x&=18\\\\x&=\\frac{9}{4}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2y&=11-3\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)\\\\2y&=\\frac{17}{4}\\\\y&=\\frac{17}{8}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{17}{8}\\right)&=7\\\\3\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{17}{8}\\right)&=11\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
