          "worked": "Double the first equation, then add the second equation to eliminate $y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10x+4y&=6\\\\13x&=17\\\\x&=\\frac{17}{13}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2y&=3-5\\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)\\\\2y&=-\\frac{46}{13}\\\\y&=-\\frac{23}{13}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck both original equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)+2\\left(-\\frac{23}{13}\\right)&=3\\\\3\\left(\\frac{17}{13}\\right)-4\\left(-\\frac{23}{13}\\right)&=11\\end{align*}$$",
